BT 1 0 0 1 0 271 Tm /F4+0 15 Tf 26 TL (Somewhere tonight there's a folding chair with nobody in it) Tj T* (yet. A warm cup of coffee, a few friendly faces, a room that) Tj T* (smells like second chances. We used to think we were too) Tj T* (smart for rooms like that. Too different. Too far gone, or) Tj T* -0.076758 Tw (not far gone enough. Then we sat down, and somebody said) Tj T* 0 Tw (out loud the thing we'd never told anyone \001 and it was our) Tj T* (story in a stranger's mouth. That's the miracle nobody) Tj T* (advertises. Not the speeches. The recognition. The moment) Tj T* (we realize we were never as alone as the disease told us.) Tj T* (The chair's still there. It doesn't care what we did. It only) Tj T* (asks one thing. Sit down. Keep coming back.) Tj T* ET
