BT 1 0 0 1 0 219 Tm -0.001578 Tw /F4+0 15 Tf 26 TL (A craving feels like it will last forever. It feels like a wall we) Tj T* 0 Tw (can't get around, a noise that won't stop until we feed it.) Tj T* (Our disease lies about that, too. Cravings rise, crest, and) Tj T* (fall \001 every single one, as long as we don't use over it. So) Tj T* (we ride it out. We tell someone. We eat something. We go) Tj T* (to group, take a walk, take a shower, pray if we pray. We) Tj T* (do anything except the one thing. And an hour later, we) Tj T* (notice it's gone, and we're still standing. That's a win.) Tj T* (Count it.) Tj T* ET
