BT 1 0 0 1 0 297 Tm /F4+0 15 Tf 26 TL (Discharge day feels like the finish line. It isn't. It's the) Tj T* (starting line, and the first few days out are when a lot of us) Tj T* (went back. Not because we wanted to. Because we walked) Tj T* (out with no plan, and the old life had one waiting for us. So) Tj T* (we build ours before we leave. Where are we sleeping the) Tj T* (first night? Who's picking us up? Where's the first meeting,) Tj T* (and what time does it start? Whose numbers are in the) Tj T* (phone? When is the first appointment with a counselor?) Tj T* (Write it down. Go over it with your counselor or sponsor. A) Tj T* (plan won't make us feel ready. It doesn't have to. It just has) Tj T* (to be there when the feeling isn't. Today, we start writing) Tj T* (ours.) Tj T* ET
